    where those two 9s each have 9s directly above them (in adjacent row), forming a vertical channel.

    More precisely: find "corner rows" (rows with 9-9-9 patterns). A 7 in a gap between corner rows
    becomes 4 if it's vertically bounded by 9s at the corner row columns.
    """
